From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: -w_port_words, the words each write port writes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per write port, a list of the words it writes. A word gets write logic
only from the ports that list it: a word written by one port takes that
port's data straight, with no data mux and no OR of the ports' write
enables, and a port builds no decoder for a word it does not list. An
array whose rows are written by fixed ports, a bank fill that writes
row r through port r, otherwise carries a data mux over every port in
every bit of every word.

A port must not address a word outside its list. Every word must be
listed by some port (RAM-0131); the lists are one per write port
(RAM-0128), name words of the array (RAM-0130), need -decoder word or
banks (RAM-0129), and no read-write port (RAM-0132).

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
